  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data, with a focus on leveraging AI for predictive analytics and data visualization. The project kicked off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial budget of $500,000 that was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. An additional $55,000 was allocated for a compliance plan. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture in September. Key milestones include a call for R&D ideas by July 20th, a staff meeting on November 20th to discuss phase two progress, and a planned launch date of March 15, 2024. Security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. The project is also exploring partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology."
